  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\nI'm creating and working on a new setup - Setup2.   However, the operation, WCS and setup from Setup1 is still visible.  This is confusing to the user.\n\nThere is no way for the user to turn off the display of Setup1 without individually turning off Setup1's WCS, stock and operations. \n\n<img width=\"1413\" height=\"955\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b7892be-2b87-4421-ab26-dd716750e966\" />\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\nEach Setup should have its own display icon and by default only the active Setup should be displayed.   It's confusing to see the the operations, WCS, etc. from a different setup at the same time.   \n\nIf the user wants to see something from a different setup allow them to turn on the display for that setup without making it active.   ",
